From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Janne Grunau <j@jannau.net>
Date: Mon, 24 Aug 2026 09:31:05 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] iommu: apple-dart: Mark DART as deferred flush capable

DART already requires explicit invalidation after domain updates so mark
it as deferred flush capable to enable DMA-FQ.

DMA-FQ improves USB4_NET iperf3 throupghput between a Apple M3 Pro
system running Linux and an Apple M1 system running macOS from

0.00-10.03  sec  1.19 GBytes  1.02 Gbits/sec                  receiver

to

0.00-10.02  sec  2.17 GBytes  1.86 Gbits/sec                  receiver

when the Linux system is the receiving system.

Signed-off-by: Janne Grunau <j@jannau.net>
(cherry picked from commit 01021f001de2789dc35177b085870d070daa1eff)
---
 drivers/iommu/apple-dart.c | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/iommu/apple-dart.c b/drivers/iommu/apple-dart.c
index 1ab6684..bd873ed 100644
--- a/drivers/iommu/apple-dart.c
+++ b/drivers/iommu/apple-dart.c
@@ -1209,6 +1209,16 @@ static struct iommu_group *apple_dart_device_group(struct device *dev)
 	return res;
 }
 
+static bool apple_dart_capable(struct device *dev, enum iommu_cap cap)
+{
+	switch (cap) {
+	case IOMMU_CAP_DEFERRED_FLUSH:
+		return true;
+	default:
+		return false;
+	}
+}
+
 static int apple_dart_def_domain_type(struct device *dev)
 {
 	struct apple_dart_master_cfg *cfg = dev_iommu_priv_get(dev);
@@ -1249,6 +1259,7 @@ static void apple_dart_get_resv_regions(struct device *dev,
 }
 
 static const struct iommu_ops apple_dart_iommu_ops = {
+	.capable = apple_dart_capable,
 	.identity_domain = &apple_dart_identity_domain,
 	.blocked_domain = &apple_dart_blocked_domain,
 	.def_domain_type = apple_dart_def_domain_type,
